# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTES AND CAVEATS
#
# HUNK 1 — confirm the ChatGPT integration path BEFORE applying.
#   `oai-authenticated-user-*` is the OpenAI Apps convention: the header is
#   injected by OpenAI's proxy. If this app is genuinely reached through that
#   proxy, stripping the header unconditionally BREAKS that sign-in flow.
#
#   Decide which case applies:
#     (a) The app is never served through the ChatGPT proxy -> apply as written;
#         /admin should move to Cloudflare Access instead (see FINDINGS-NEW.md).
#     (b) The app IS served through the proxy -> keep the hunk, and configure
#         TRUSTED_PROXY_SECRET plus the matching header on the proxy side. If the
#         proxy cannot send a custom header, use Cloudflare mTLS or an Access
#         service token instead and gate on that rather than a shared secret.
#
#   Either way, do NOT set ADMIN_EMAILS until one of these is in place — that
#   binding is currently the only thing keeping the bypass closed (NF-3).
#
#   The `new Request(request, { headers })` clone matches the pattern vinext
#   already uses at this entry point (cloneRequestWithHeaders), so it is safe in
#   the Workers runtime.
#
# HUNK 3 — `preload` is a commitment, not just a header.
#   Do NOT ship this until every subdomain of cfbapex.com is confirmed
#   HTTPS-only, because includeSubDomains + preload will break any plaintext
#   subdomain. Removal from the preload list takes months. Ship hunks 1-2 first
#   and treat hunk 3 as a separate, deliberate step, then submit the domain at
#   https://hstspreload.org.
#
# Not addressed here — audit Issue 4 (CSP still allows 'unsafe-inline' for
# script-src and style-src). That needs the render pipeline to emit a nonce on
# every inline tag, which is not safely patchable from the compiled bundle.
# See patches/REMAINING-FIXES.md.
